      "title": "Post-doctoral Software Engineer for the Compliance AI Regulatory Assistant (CARA) project",
      "description": "Post-doctoral Software Engineer for the Compliance AI Regulatory Assistant (CARA) project Vacancy Description : This is a software engineering position in the Regulated Software Research Centre (RSRC) within the School of Informatics and Creative Arts in DkIT. The successful candidate will join the Compliance AI Regulatory Assistant (CARA) project. This project is supported by the Enterprise Ireland Commercialisation Fund Programme through project CF-2026-3089-F. The RSRC is recognized as a world-class research group within the area of medical device software engineering. Since its creation in 2008 the RSRC has been highly successful in attracting competitive external funding. The RSRC currently has a number of ongoing software engineering research projects within the domains of Medical Devices, Artificial Intelligence, Software Regulations, Software Process and Safety Critical Systems. The position is being created as result of the RSRC obtaining research funding through Commercialisation fund, funded by Enterprise Ireland. The project will develop a regulatory compliance platform for medical device manufacturers. AI has huge potential benefits within the healthcare domain, but a significant challenge exists in that healthcare remains an inherently risk-adverse domain. At this time, regulators are working to develop additional standards and guidance that will help developers advance AI capabilities in the healthcare domain. The number of standards in the medical device domain can pose additional challenges and expenses for manufacturers in this field, particularly SMEs and start-ups. The CARA platform will help manufacturers address these regulatory challenges by assisting compliance with the required standards and regulations, thereby accelerating product development and market entry. Job Title : Post Doc Research Vacancy ID : 016218 Vacancy Type : Academic"
    }
  },
